course: dictionary
lesson: 446
title: Area: flat space or a part of a place
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Area has two main meanings. The first is how much flat space a shape covers, and we measure it in squares, such as square metres. The second is a part of a place, such as a play area or a picnic area.
explain: Look at the words around the word to choose the right meaning. «Russia is the largest country by area, and Canada is the second largest» is about how much land each country covers. «Wombats leave droppings to mark their area» is about the part of a place where they live.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If you read «a large area around it» and think of a part of a place, it still makes sense. If you think of a flat shape, it does not.
fact: Area means how much flat space a shape covers.
fact: For a rectangle, area = length × width, and the answer is written in square units, such as square centimetres.
fact: «Square units» tells you the answer is counted in squares, not in plain centimetres.
fact: An area can also be a part of a place, such as a «picnic area» or a «local area».
fact: «Wombats are the only animals known to make cube-shaped droppings», and they leave them on rocks and logs to mark their area.
exercise: «A rectangle is 8 cm long and 5 cm wide. What is its area?» | *40 square centimetres | 13 square centimetres | 5 square centimetres | 26 square centimetres
exercise: «Wombats leave droppings on rocks and logs to mark their area.» What does area mean here? | Length plus width | *A part of a place where they live | The sound a loud noise makes | The number of wombats in the group
exercise: A flat shape's area is measured in which units? | degrees | kilograms | *square metres | litres
test: «Russia is the largest country by area.» What does area mean here? | The weather in winter | The height of its mountains | The number of people who live there | *How much land a country covers
test: A rectangle has a length of 6 cm and a width of 4 cm. What is its area? | 12 square centimetres | 10 square centimetres | *24 square centimetres | 20 centimetres
exam: «A large-scale map, such as 1:25,000, shows a small area in great detail.» Which map shows a huge area with little detail? | *A small-scale map, such as 1:10,000,000 | A large-scale map, such as 1:25,000 | A map of the playground | A map with no scale at all
